<article class="env-theorem" id="06Q5">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06Q5">Theorem <span data-tag="06Q5">9.5.2.1</span> <span class="named">(Adjoint Functor Theorem)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be presentable $\infty $-categories. Then: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
A functor $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ admits a right adjoint if and only if it preserves small colimits. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
A functor $G: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits a left adjoint if and only if it is accessible and preserves small limits. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof of Theorem <a data-tag="06Q5" href="/tag/06Q5">9.5.2.1</a>.</strong>
       Combine Propositions <a data-tag="06QB" href="/tag/06QB">9.5.2.2</a> and <a data-tag="06QC" href="/tag/06QC">9.5.2.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
